Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:07.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Put your hand on your chest. This muscle, the size of your fist, beats about 100,000 times a day… without ever taking a break.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.29,0:00:19.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,The heart is two pumps stuck together. The right half sends blood to the lungs to pick up oxygen. The left half, more muscular, sends it around the whole body.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.87,0:00:24.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,At rest, about five litres per minute: roughly all of your blood, in one minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.91,0:00:34.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,And who sets the rhythm? A small spot at the top of the heart: the sinus node. It sends an electrical signal. The atria contract… then the ventricles.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.22,0:00:37.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the famous "lub-dub" is the sound of the valves closing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.92,0:00:49.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,At rest, an adult usually has between 60 and 100 beats per minute. Above that, it's called tachycardia. Often it's normal: exercise, emotion, fever, too much coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.33,0:00:53.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But sometimes it's an electrical short circuit: the heart races for no reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.52,0:01:01.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Below 60, it's bradycardia. In an athlete, it's often a good sign: their stronger heart pumps more blood with each beat.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.77,0:01:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if the electrical signal gets blocked on the way, the heart slows down too much: tiredness, dizziness, fainting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.71,0:01:14.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,To keep it in shape: move at least two and a half hours a week, don't smoke, eat less salt, sleep well and keep an eye on your blood pressure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.92,0:01:23.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when the heart stops? Blood no longer flows. Deprived of oxygen, the brain loses consciousness within seconds, and starts to be damaged after a few minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.69,0:01:27.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why chest compressions and a defibrillator, right away, can save a life.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.39,0:01:32.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you, would you know how to do chest compressions? Tell me in the comments.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.69,0:00:10.49,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(300,500)\c&H7797D9&}TON CŒUR BAT\N100 000 FOIS PAR JOUR\N{\fs60\c&HFFFFFF&\b0}Your heart beats 100,000 times a day
